   208	        due_day = (NOT_MEASURED, {'theses whose three sends are ladders': len(all_ladders), 'needed': 20})
   209	    else:
   210	        same = [case for case in all_ladders if len({o['view']['due_day'] for o in sends_of[case]}) == 1]      # the day the question is due (D414)
   211	        due_day = ('met' if len(same) * 10 >= len(all_ladders) * 9 else 'missed', {'theses': len(all_ladders), 'same due day': len(same)})
   212	    report['lines'][6] = {'direction': direction, 'due day': due_day, 'shape differs across sends': shape_differs}
   213	
   214	    if measured:
   215	        populations = {mark: ladders for mark in LADDER_MARKS}
   287	## 12. Close-out (2026-11-08)
   288	
   289	**Alex's decisions (2026-11-08):**
   290	- a record that is a repeat of several groups joins only the one Jev judges it most like (the highest same_statement probability; ties
   291	  go to the earliest group);
   292	- the Step 2 lines: (1) search at least 90%; (2) clear wrong merges at most 2%; (3) grouped dossiers keep no fewer later details than
   293	  no merging.
   294	
   295	Both are recorded in PRD §5.
   296	
   297	**Built.**
   298	- `clean-arch/step2/compare.py`: search, Jev comparison, the outcome with best match, forward order, and a failed comparison refused and
   299	  reported. `test_compare.py`: 6 tests; all 4 mutants caught.
   300	- `run_forward.py` reads a stored Step 1 trace directly.
   301	- **Run** (`poc/data/clean-step2-forward-2026-11-08/`, a fresh Jev draw): 282 records made 178 groups.
   302	  - 104 repeats, 3 revisions, 0 refused; 16 records had several same_statement answers.
   303	  - The cached embedding texts were verified identical: 282 of 282 documents, 313 of 313 queries.
   304	
   305	**Council A** (`council/group/d-*`):
   306	- report search as recall over known labelled counterparts;
   307	- blind-review every merge, previously labelled positives included;
   308	- verify the cache texts;
   309	- re-run the reader test on the new views.
   310	
   311	| Line | Result | Met |
   312	|---|---|---|
   313	| 1. Search | 112/113 known labelled counterparts had a holding group among the candidates (99.1%). For 107 of them the group's original, which is what Jev saw, is itself a counterpart. This is not recall over all real repeats. | yes |
   314	| 2. Clear wrong merges | 104 merges read by two blind readers; 85 accepted by both; the 19 rejected by either went to a third reader: acceptable 1, overlap 15, **wrong 3** = 2.9% | **no** (missed by one merge) |
   315	| 3. Later details | Reader test re-run on the rebuilt views with the frozen questions and key: detail none 27.5, source 3, group **28** of 36; unsupported claims 3 / 2 / 2; double counting 0 | yes |
