    59	## 1. Before acting on a failure: diagnose
    60	
    61	A failure is a question, not a task. Nothing changes (code, prompt, configuration, test, gold) until these are written:
    62	
    63	1. **The class.** Count every instance on stored data, at no cost: how many, since when, what each costs; never only the case in view.
    64	   Match by path or field, not by substring, and check the census on one case whose answer is known. A flagged word in a document is a
    65	   class too: count it over the whole scope before the first edit.
    66	2. **The mechanism.** Trace one case end to end (the raw output, every check that dropped it, the input that produced it, the code
    67	   that built that input) to the design choice that produces the whole class. First check whether your own last change or load caused
    68	   it; when several mechanisms stack on the same cases, find them all first.
    69	3. **Step back.** Is it the product's problem, or one the measurement or process made? Read the governing standard and the decisions on
    70	   the topic before writing any rule: the answer is often written already, and a question about the measuring stick is answered by the
    71	   frozen ruler (§7.1), never by a new ruler (Alex, 2026-10-29: "我们是聊过这个事情的你难道没看文档吗").

codex
**V2 is still not ready.** The clearest example is the input proof. The helper still compares sorted IDs, then gives the clean reader the production order. Adding a database argument would let both systems read the filtered copy, but it would not prove that both actual launches read the same articles in the same order. [Input helper](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/fresh_week_inputs.py:43) · [V2 input proof](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:62)

1. **Round-one findings still open.** Prove ordered IDs and text through both real entry points, including an excluded article. Use each invocation’s cutoff for the judge. V2 specifies September 20, but the slice ends July 7. The 6,000-attempt allowance is a valid stop if intentional, but it is not a worst-case retry bound. A format retry can itself make three network attempts. The cited astra wrapper also omits the shared ledger. The new wrapper must preserve reservation and stop enforcement on every attempt. Finally, triage promises a first-scored-week checkpoint that v2 does not contain. The judge’s recent-history rule still admits all qualifying new arrivals, so it does not bound request size. Add a stored-data size check and a late-stage monitoring threshold. [V2 launcher and slice](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:141) · [Format retry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/runner.py:323) · [Network retry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/live.py:82) · [Astra wrapper](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/gate1-candidate/gate1_candidate.py:94) · [Triage checkpoint](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/triage-1.md:15) · [Judge evidence selection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:41)

2. **The two decisions.** **Count independently eligible financial matters in `N`.** D665 counts every listed matter, and D431 compares the products as configured. D505 still says the new system should use the company’s own figures as evidence. The blind list must therefore distinguish a worthwhile question from a figure worth filing. Print the subgroup so Alex can see how much of the result comes from that policy. **The sealed-replay exception needs an explicit decision.** D613 describes what its Step 1 census checked. It does not define “unread” for either system. Exempt a sealed replay only where the record supports ordinary replay use. An article can inform tuning without being named in a decision. Query structured archives and traces, including binary and ignored files, and require a known-hit control. `rg -F -f` alone cannot establish absence. [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9410) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795) · [D505](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5835) · [D613](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8197) · [V2 census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:42)

3. **The reading can still move the verdict.** `council_mark.py` is tied to Deck 1 and asserts **19 cards**. Its support marks also lack a distinct *insufficient* value. Provide a comparison input and freeze how missing answers, insufficient evidence, disputes, and duplicate questions enter each denominator and minimum. Require an explicit rejection on every plant. V2’s wording could let “cannot tell” slip through as a plant that was never accepted. Freeze what happens if a week has fewer than 40 eligible articles. [Deck builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/pilot-deck-1/council-marking/council_mark.py:60) · [Allowed marks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/pilot-deck-1/council-marking/council_mark.py:132) · [V2 credit and controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:114) · [Sampling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:72)

4. **Monitoring still lacks the denominator for its stop.** Settled attempts include retries and failed sends. The attempt log is also best-effort. It cannot supply completed clean articles for the 2× rule. Add completed-article and completed-judge-day progress, then compare each component with its own baseline. The Step 1 slice baseline is rebased, but it cannot price late judging. Keep D449’s explicit redo authorization. A stopped ledger does not by itself authorize six fresh draws. [V2 monitor](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:239) · [Attempt log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:99) · [D449](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4937) · [D666 scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9443)

5. **Required reports still differ from D665.** D400 line 5 needs all three passes. The date check is agreement across all three sends for at least 90% of eligible **questions**, not agreement in 90% of passes. The July frozen-reference readout needs both systems and the unseeded question mapping, not Stage B on the new system alone. Step 2’s old method needs reference counterparts, merge judgments, and the no-merge detail comparison. Name those inputs before launch. The two source-based floors remain explicitly unmeasured. Get agreement on that reporting gap before the run. [V2 check table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:156) · [D400 accounting](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/accounting.py:188) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795) · [Step 2 method](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:305)

**NOT READY: prove identical inputs and cutoff through both launchers, settle the exposure exception, freeze the comparison reader and scorer, and make the required checks and monitoring executable.**
